@page "/HowItWorks/return-of-capital"
@using InvestmentTaxCalculator.Components

<HowItWorksGuideLayout PageAddress="HowItWorks/return-of-capital">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="section">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Interactive Brokers cash entries described as "Return of Capital" are imported as a return of capital,
                    dated on the settlement date.
                </li>
                <li>
                    They are not counted as dividend income. They appear on the
                    <a href="DividendDataPage" class="link-styled">Dividend/Income Data</a> page with the type "Return of
                    Capital" so you can see them.
                </li>
                <li>
                    On that date, the amount in pounds is deducted from the cost of the share's Section 104 pool. The number of
                    shares does not change, and nothing is matched or disposed of.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The lower cost means a larger gain, or a smaller loss, when you later sell from the pool. You can follow
                    the change on the <a href="Section104DataPage" class="link-styled">Section 104 Data</a> page.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h5 card-title">Worked example</h2>
                <p class="mb-0">
                    Your pool holds 100 shares costing £2,000 when the company returns £150 of capital. The pool becomes 100
                    shares costing <strong>£1,850</strong>. If you later sell all 100 for £2,500, the gain is £650.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
    <FurtherReading>
        <li><a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1992/12/section/122" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TCGA 1992 s122</a>: capital distributions</li>
        <li><a href="HowItWorks/section-104-pool" class="link-styled">Section 104 pool</a></li>
    </FurtherReading>
</HowItWorksGuideLayout>
